WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(applause)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.500
Now, Jason, congratulations,

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.660
of course you're getting
a lot of attention

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.280
for your Joe Biden impression

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.113
on Saturday Night Live.

00:00:06.113 --> 00:00:06.946
Thank you, thank you very much.

00:00:06.946 --> 00:00:08.490
Did you always do a Joe Biden

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.540
For years.
When you were a kid?

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:11.970
For years.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.070
How did you have to
work on this impression?

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.190
Literally, we did one last year

00:00:17.648 --> 00:00:19.140
for the Halloween shows him

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.730
dressed up for something.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.750
And so I just did three lines

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.490
and then over the summer

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.470
when he was named the
vice president nominee,

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:28.920
I remembered that I was doing Joe Biden.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:29.753
That I had done him

00:00:29.753 --> 00:00:31.050
because I got a text
from people at the show

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.460
saying "Hey, congrats".

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:33.300
I was like, "congrats"?

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.133
Why?

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.700
Oh, oh right, I do Joe Biden.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:36.533
Sure.

00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:40.010
So then, I watched a lot of YouTube

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.390
throughout this last week to sort of

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:42.393
try to study him.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.130
It's all the teeth.

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:46.830
It's all teeth.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.280
Like, I don't have Joe Biden teeth.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.130
Like, when I smile.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.740
Like, if I just smile normally.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.480
You know, it's all gums.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:55.780
You get a lot of gum, yeah.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:56.880
No teeth whatsoever.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.690
So then they were very nice.
I even brought them with me

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:00.850
cause I carry them all the time.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:03.170
I ride with them on the subway.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:04.570
But look at this right here.

00:01:07.574 --> 00:01:08.407
There they are.

00:01:08.407 --> 00:01:09.604
(Conan and audience laughs and applauds)

00:01:09.604 --> 00:01:10.437
There he is.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:11.270
(applause)

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.103
Those are overpowering.

00:01:12.103 --> 00:01:12.936
I know.

00:01:12.936 --> 00:01:13.769
Turn those off.

00:01:13.769 --> 00:01:14.602
There he is.

00:01:14.602 --> 00:01:15.435
Look at that.

00:01:15.435 --> 00:01:16.730
Oh, man.

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:18.560
You get this to show
up on a wide angle too.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:19.720
Look at that, hey!

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.150
Those are beautiful, yeah.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:21.983
Not bad, right?

00:01:21.983 --> 00:01:25.710
Now, did you get a lot of
feedback on that sketch?

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:26.611
I did, yeah.

00:01:26.611 --> 00:01:27.640
You know, we just watched
a little clip of it.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.090
Yeah, I mean, from like
friends out of nowhere.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:32.370
Most of it positive.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.260
I did however get one guy
that was a little upset at me.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:38.092
I actually have it here on MySpace.

00:01:38.092 --> 00:01:38.925
Everybody has MySpace, right?

00:01:38.925 --> 00:01:39.760
You know MySpace.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:40.593
Right.

00:01:40.593 --> 00:01:41.900
People can get ahold of ya.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.390
and let you know their feelings.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:45.150
What was it that bothered him?

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.900
It was the run there about
Scranton, Pennsylvania.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:50.510
About it being a jerk wad of a town.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:51.500
Is he from Scranton?

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.040
Yeah, I'm guessing that's where he's from.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:55.053
His name's Pete.

00:01:55.977 --> 00:01:56.810
This is real.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:57.720
This really happened.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.392
The subject was "Eat me".

00:01:59.392 --> 00:02:01.190
(audience laughs)

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:03.017
And then this is what he says:

00:02:03.017 --> 00:02:04.690
"If you have a problem with Scranton,

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.450
why don't you come out
and say it to my face,

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.607
you (bleep) no-talent hack".

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:12.763
Fair hit.

00:02:12.763 --> 00:02:13.596
Yeah.

00:02:14.733 --> 00:02:16.633
I get a lot of these.
Yeah, I believe it.

00:02:17.627 --> 00:02:20.020
"It's funny that I had
to see the Scranton skit

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:21.060
on the Internet since I thought

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.910
SNL was canceled years ago.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:23.950
Turns out, it's still on.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:24.835
It just sucks.

00:02:24.835 --> 00:02:26.540
(audience laughs)

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.890
Why don't you take a long
swim in the East river?

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:29.723
Before you do, be sure to strap

00:02:29.723 --> 00:02:33.030
200 lbs of bricks on your
back before you jump in".

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:33.920
But then it signs off

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.192
(bleeps) bite me you (bleep).

00:02:36.192 --> 00:02:39.025
(audience laughs)

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:41.453
There's Pete right there.

00:02:41.453 --> 00:02:42.286
There's Pete.

00:02:42.286 --> 00:02:43.663
Let's see Pete.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:44.496
Look at that.

00:02:44.496 --> 00:02:48.413
(audience laughs and applauds)

00:02:51.799 --> 00:02:53.080
Nice looking guy!

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.930
I love how, like he wrote that (growls).

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:57.780
Then it's like time for
a photo to go with that.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:58.762
Oh, okay.

00:02:58.762 --> 00:03:00.290
(audience laughs)

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.390
I'm gonna put on my best duds.

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:02.223
Yeah.

00:03:02.223 --> 00:03:03.180
I mean, he looks like a really nice guy.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:05.180
And I can't bolt him for loving his town.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:07.560
I mean, obviously, I do want to say

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:11.860
Pete, in all sincerity,
I've never been to Scranton,

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.350
but I respect the fact that you like it

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.810
and I'm sorry for
upsetting you in any way.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:17.980
I actually did not write that.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:21.400
The writer that did,
here's his email address.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.600
It's ScrantonSucksBigOne

00:03:23.492 --> 00:03:24.551
(silence)

00:03:24.551 --> 00:03:26.698
(audience laughs)

00:03:26.698 --> 00:03:28.031
That's the best way.

00:03:28.031 --> 00:03:29.041
Just go right to him.

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:32.940
(audience applauds and cheers)

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.286
His name's Petey.

00:03:34.286 --> 00:03:35.250
His name's Petey.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:39.240
Now, of course Tina Fey
getting a lot of attention

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.310
for her governor panel, which
is a great governor panel.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.110
Absolutely, no, I mean,
she needs the dough.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.200
She had a comeback and
needed it, you know.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.979
She was desperate for that part.

00:03:47.979 --> 00:03:50.550
Didn't even look anything
like her, but it's sad.

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:51.383
No, it's fantastic.

00:03:51.383 --> 00:03:53.490
It's such a buzzsaw as they

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:54.956
stay in sports to be up there.

00:03:54.956 --> 00:03:56.100
It's so nerve-wracking.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.611
I was like, she's so great at it

00:03:57.611 --> 00:04:00.347
and looks just like her
and sounds just like her

00:04:00.347 --> 00:04:01.550
and it's such a fun take on her.

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:04.010
And I was like oh, I
hope that this doesn't go

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.400
as I'm thinking it might

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.950
where she says stuff and everybody laughs

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:09.350
and then I say stuff,
nobody says anything.

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.183
Not even looking at me.

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:11.970
Just waiting for her to
talk again or something.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:12.803
It would be awful.

00:04:12.803 --> 00:04:13.670
People love the teeth.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:14.750
They love the teeth.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:16.923
Now, I'm curious about something.

00:04:18.863 --> 00:04:20.470
When I worked Saturday
Night Live years ago,

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:21.840
one of the best things
is all the cool people

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.030
that would show up to do it.
Here you are, you guys are

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.010
satirizing the presidential campaign

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.980
and these people actually show up.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:29.940
Have you gotten a chance to really meet

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:32.759
or get to know Barack
Obama or John McCain?

00:04:32.759 --> 00:04:34.110
I don't know if I got to
know them, necessarily.

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:35.776
I mean, I get it, I get it. I get it.

00:04:37.509 --> 00:04:39.963
After you said that meant
"It's okay, I got it".

00:04:39.963 --> 00:04:40.796
I get it.

00:04:40.796 --> 00:04:42.220
No, no, no it's all right.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:44.450
I met Barack Obama that same sketch

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.500
where I was dressed as Joe Biden.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:47.830
We met him.

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:49.710
They're a real nice guy.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:50.543
Good eye contact.

00:04:50.543 --> 00:04:51.483
Good handshake.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:53.390
Looks good in a suit.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:54.383
Yep.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:56.193
Check.

00:04:56.193 --> 00:04:57.097
Exactly.

00:04:57.097 --> 00:04:57.930
I got it.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.330
All three boxes checked.

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:01.620
And then John McCain was on last year.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:03.510
And in between the dress show

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:05.480
which we do before the live show,

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:07.500
there's a meeting in Lauren's' office.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.740
And it's like 50 of us all sitting around.

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:10.573
You may remember this.

00:05:10.573 --> 00:05:11.440
In a tiny room.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:12.830
People are all like squeezed in.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:13.760
I sit on a stair,

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:15.870
like on a step like this down here.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.040
Really copping a squat.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.916
Literally it looks like
I'm about to take a dump.

00:05:19.916 --> 00:05:23.957
(audience laughs) You
know what I mean right?

00:05:23.957 --> 00:05:24.790
Why, why?

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:25.640
That's just the position I'm in.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:26.830
Yes, okay thanks.

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:27.870
But it's only funny because

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:30.500
at this point, John
McCain comes walking over

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:31.600
cause there's an empty
spot right next to me.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:32.720
Sits right down next to me.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.470
Like, we're like two
little kids with our knees

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:35.610
like right by our chin.

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:37.340
And I'm wearing KU basketball shorts.

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:38.610
Kansas University basketball shorts,

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:39.670
which I wear in-between the shows

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:41.150
just because it's comfortable.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:43.820
And he starts talking
to me about you know,

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.950
Kansas basketball and
like, Arizona basketball

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:48.830
and Luke Olsen, I think
was their coach there.

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:49.710
And all this stuff.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:51.750
Anyway, we're talking while Lauren

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.340
is giving our bosses, is giving us notes,

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:54.370
trying to tell us the changes

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:56.180
that are about to happen to the live show.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:57.610
Lauren can be intimidating
in this meeting.

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:58.600
Oh, extremely intimidating.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:00.600
He's making quick changes

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:02.180
30 minutes before this
thing's about to go out

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:03.370
to millions and millions of people.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:05.287
And John McCain is just like

00:06:05.287 --> 00:06:09.570
"How about the KU Jayhawks and Luke Olsen"

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:11.500
and I'm like we're gonna get busted.

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:13.060
Like, you can't.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.520
We're supposed to be
paying attention, sir.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:17.670
But then I realized I'm
not gonna get in trouble.

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:19.340
Lauren's not gonna yell at John McCain.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:21.620
I'm in the clear. I was
like, do you want to share

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:23.580
what you're talking about
to the rest of the class?

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:25.140
I was like, we're talking
about foreign policy.

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:26.220
Leave us alone.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:27.540
Don't worry about it.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:29.283
We're figuring it out.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:33.043
Worry about your silly skits.

00:06:35.002 --> 00:06:37.302
[Conan] Now, I wish I
had been there for that.

